`_interaction_tool_definitions` serializes tools unconditionally on every fetched interaction. Move it inside `if telemetry_handler.should_capture_content():` to skip this work when content capture is off:

```suggestion
    if telemetry_handler.should_capture_content():
        invocation.tool_definitions = _interaction_tool_definitions(response)
        messages = _interactions_response_to_messages(
            response, finish_reason=None
        )
        if streamed_parts and not _has_content(messages):
            messages = _streamed_output_messages(streamed_parts)
        invocation.output_messages = messages
        if system_instruction := _get_field(response, "system_instruction"):
            invocation.system_instruction = [
                TextPart(content=system_instruction)
            ]
```

`GenAiError` from `_gaos` provides `status_code: int`. Updating `resolve_error_type` in `_error_type.py` to check `getattr(exc, "status_code", None)` allows reporting the HTTP status code (e.g. `"404"`) per semconv instead of the qualified class name:

```python
def resolve_error_type(exc: BaseException) -> str | None:
    if isinstance(exc, genai_errors.APIError):
        return str(exc.code)
    if (status_code := getattr(exc, "status_code", None)) is not None:
        return str(status_code)
    return None
```

